            <h1>Aerosol Valve Gasket Materials Explained: Chemistry, Compatibility & Failure Prevention</h1>
        </div>
        <p>Aerosol valves are precision-engineered systems where even the smallest component can determine product success or failure. Among these components, the valve gasket plays a decisive role in sealing, pressure retention, chemical resistance, and long-term reliability. Despite its importance, gasket selection is often treated as a commodity decision rather than a chemistry-driven engineering choice.</p>
        <p>This article explains aerosol valve gasket materials from a scientific and engineering perspective, focusing strictly on established material science, elastomer chemistry, and real-world compatibility data. The objective is to help startups, students, and product developers prevent failures, reduce recalls, and design aerosols that perform consistently across markets and climates.</p>
        <figure>
            <img src="https://assets.zyrosite.com/A3QlOV94WLSaL6xE/aerosol-valve-gasket-cross-section-t5Mg7GX97TASNqRU.png" alt="Cross-sectional diagram of an aerosol valve highlighting the gasket position" loading="lazy">
